=== history-blob {#b210 lang=geml}
A hyphen keeps an extension out of this specification's way; it does not tell a
processor what the name means, and §8.2(6) still requires the name to degrade to
a warning. `profile` is how a document says which extensions it is using. The
key is declared in `=== meta` and holds a space-separated list of **vocabulary
names**:

